    "title": "Breast cancer survivor wins $2 million from Pennsylvania Lottery - NewsBreak",
    "text": "ERIE, Pa. ( WJET/WFXP ) — A Warren County breast cancer survivor’s luck has turned around in a big way! Nicole Walter is the winner of $2 million from the Pennsylvania Lottery. She was presented with a commemorative check in front of her family, including 10 grandchildren, at the lottery office in Erie on Wednesday. Walter won playing the online Monopoly-themed game. The 42-year-old recently completed radiation treatment, during which she suffered a heart attack. She called the lottery win life-changing. “It could have never come at a better time. It was a great time to come,” she told us. “There was a lot of prayers coming for days before cause things were looking a little bleak there for a while. And now it’s just so stress relieving, really.” Walter said she has been playing the lottery online since it launched in 2018, but this is her first win. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ABC27.",
